  "lineage": "Cuban troubadour-song tradition emerging in late-nineteenth-century Santiago de Cuba and Havana from synthesis of Spanish romance ballad with Cuban son and bolero. Solo voice or duo with one or two acoustic guitars, intimate-confessional register. Trova tradicional (1890s-1920s, Sindo Garay, Manuel Corona) crystallized the genre; nueva trova (post-1968, Silvio Rodríguez, Pablo Milanés) integrated revolutionary-political content.",
